From 5fe63e9d54a09b590cc494712bfa1bf9b7e6c9fb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Henry Wu <Henry_Wu@quantatw.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 17:50:13 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] platform-mc: drop stale discovery work on endpoint removal

Track MCTP endpoint generations for queued discovery batches
and mark endpoints stale when removal is reported. Remove
stale entries from the pending discovery queue, cancel
requester operations for removed EIDs, and avoid using
termini that were initialized after their endpoint
disappeared.

Limit post-discovery platform initialization to TIDs added
by the current batch and re-check terminus liveness across
awaits. This prevents a removed endpoint from keeping
discoverMctpTerminusTask and follow-on queues blocked.

The link of upstream:
https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/pldm/+/95350

Signed-off-by: Henry Wu <Henry_Wu@quantatw.com>
